            <ArticleTitle>Left atrial thrombosis associated with antipsychotic drugs.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>153-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case of a 36-year-old shizophrenic patient with left atrial thrombosis. There have been small number of case reports of antipsychotic drugs-associated thromboembolic events. All of them are venous ones. This paper describes the first case of atrial thrombosis associated with antipsychotic drugs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
